+ OB₁^2 \\quad \\Rightarrow \\quad OB₁^2 = 16 \\quad \\Rightarrow \\quad OB₁ = 4 \\text{ cm}\n\\]\n\nNext, since point D is the midpoint of AB and now falls on A₁B₁ such that D₁B₁ is similar to the original configuration, where D₁D (which is D₁B₁) equals the length of AD.\n\nTo find \\( B₁D \\), recognize that it forms a similar right triangle with the original △AOB, adjusted by rotation:\n\n\\[\nB₁D = \\frac{BO + A₁D}{2} = \\frac{4 + 3}{2} = \\frac{7}{2} \\text{ cm}\n\\]\n\n</think> <answer> \\frac{7}{2} </answer>']
