( f(x) \\), the equation \\( \\sqrt{(2 + \\sqrt{3})^x} + \\sqrt{(2 - \\sqrt{3})^x} = 4 \\) has exactly one solution, which is \\( x = 1 \\).\n\n</think><answer> $1$ </answer> </think></think></answer></think></think></answer></think></think></think></think></think></think></think></think></think></think></think></think></think></think></think></think></think></think></think></think></think></think></think></think></think></think></think></think></think></think></think></think></think></think></think></think></think></think></think></think></think></think></think></think></think></think></think></think></think></think></think></think></think></think></think></think></think></think></think></think></think></think></think></think></think></think></think></think></think></think></think></think></think></think></think></think></think></think></think></think></think></think></think></think></think></think></think></think></think></think></think></think></think></think></think></think></think></think></think></think></think></think></think></think></think></think></think></think></think></think></think></think></think></think></think></think></think></think></think></think></think></think></think></think></think></think></think></think></think></think></think></think></think></think></think></think></think></think></think></think></think></think></think></think></think></think></think></think></think></think></think></think></think></think></think></think></think></think></think></think></think></think></think></think></think></think></think></think></think></think></think></think></think></think></think></think></think></think></think></think></think></think></think></think></think></think></think></think></think></think></think></think></think></think></think></think></think></think></think></think></think></think></think></think></think></think></think></think></think></think></think></think></think></think></think></think></think></think></think></think></think></think