[36m(ActorModelRayActor pid=1324, ip=10.252.164.17)[0m ['  system\n你是书生·万象，英文名是InternVL，是由上海人工智能实验室、清华大学及多家合作单位联合开发的多模态大语言模型。 \n user\n\nYou should first thinks about the reasoning process in the mind and then provides the user with the answer. Your answer must be in latex format and wrapped in $...$.The reasoning process and answer are enclosed within <think> </think> and <answer> </answer> tags, respectively, i.e., <think> Since $1+1=2$, so the answer is $2$. </think><answer> $2$ </answer>, which means your output should start with <think> and end with </answer>.\nQuestion:\nWhat is the range of the function $$F(x) = |x+1|+|x-5|~?$$Express your answer in interval notation. \nassistant\n<think> To determine the range of the function \\( F(x) = |x+1| + |x-5| \\), we need to analyze how the function behaves for different values of \\( x \\). The function involves absolute values, which change behavior at the points where the expressions inside the absolute values are zero. These points are \\( x = -1 \\) and \\( x = 5 \\). We will consider the intervals defined by these points: \\( x < -1 \\), \\( -1 \\leq x \\leq 5 \\), and \\( x > 5 \\).\n\n1. **For \\( x < -1 \\)**:\n   - \\( |x+1| = -(x+1) = -x-1 \\)\n   - \\( |x-5| = -(x-5) = -x+5 \\)\n   - Therefore, \\( F(x) = (-x-1) + (-x+5) = -2x + 4 \\)\n   - As \\( x \\) decreases, \\( -2x + 4 \\) increases, so \\( F(x) \\) is increasing in this interval.\n\n2. **For \\( -1 \\leq x \\leq 5 \\)**:\n   - \\( |x+1| = x+1 \\)\n   - \\( |x-5| = -(x-5) = -x+5 \\)\n   - Therefore, \\( F(x) = (x+1) + (-x+5) = 6 \\)\n   - This is a constant function with value 6 in this interval.\n\n3. **For \\( x > 5 \\)**:\n   - \\( |x+1| = x+1 \\)\n   - \\( |x-5| = x-5 \\)\n   - Therefore, \\( F(x) = (x+1) + (x-5) = 2x - 4 \\)\n   - As \\( x \\) increases, \\( 2x - 4 \\) increases, so \\( F(x) \\) is increasing in this interval.\n\nNext, we evaluate the function at the critical points \\( x = -1 \\) and \\( x = 5 \\):\n- At \\( x = -1 \\), \\( F(-1) = |-1+1| + |-1-5| = 0 + 6 = 6 \\)\n- At \\( x = 5 \\), \\( F(5) = |5+1| + |5-5| = 6 + 0 = 6 \\)\n\nThe function is continuous and the values are:\n- For \\( x < -1 \\), \\( F(x) \\) increases from \\( \\infty \\) to 6.\n- For \\( -1 \\leq x \\leq 5 \\), \\( F(x) = 6 \\).\n- For \\( x > 5 \\), \\( F(x) \\) increases from 6 to \\( \\infty \\).\n\nThus, the range of \\( F(x) \\) is all values greater than or equal to 6, expressed in interval notation as \\( [6, \\infty) \\). </think><answer> $[6, \\infty)$ </answer> </think> </answer> </think> </answer> </think> </answer> </think> </answer> </think> </answer> </think> </answer> </think> </answer> </think> </answer> </think> </answer> </think> </answer> </think> </answer> </think> </answer> </think> </answer> </think> </answer> </think> </answer> </think> </answer> </think> </answer> </think> </answer> </think> </answer> </think> </answer> </think> </answer> </think> </answer> </think> </answer> </think> </answer> </think> </answer> </think> </answer> </think> </answer> </think> </answer> </think> </answer> </think> </answer> </think> </answer> </think> </answer> </think> </answer> </think> </answer> </think> </answer> </think> </answer> </think> </answer> </think> </answer> </think> </answer> </think> </answer> </think> </answer> </think> </answer> </think> </answer> </think> </answer> </think> </answer> </think> </answer> </think> </answer> </think> </answer> </think> </answer> </think> </answer> </think> </answer> </think> </answer> </think> </answer> </think> </answer> </think> </answer> </think> </answer> </think> </answer> </think> </answer> </think> </answer> </think> </answer> </think> </answer> </think> </answer> </think> </answer> </think> </answer> </think> </answer> </think> </answer> </think> </answer> </think> </answer> </think> </answer> </think> </answer> </think> </answer> </think> </answer> </think> </answer> </think> </answer> </think> </answer> </think> </answer> </think> </answer> </think> </